# examples/scenes/01_stack, played: a game paused and resumed, and given up
# from the pause menu. Every transition is deferred to the end of the frame
# that asks for it, so `expect scene` is the scene on top once that frame is
# over. See tests/e2e/script.h for the grammar.

# --- the happy path: play, pause, resume ------------------------------------

# Play has the focus from the first frame: Enter alone presses it.
1 tap KEY_ENTER
1 expect scene GameScene

# Ten points a second. Pause with the mouse: down on 41, up on 42, and the
# pause menu is pushed on top at the end of 42.
40 shot playing
41 click 70 105
41 expect scene GameScene
42 expect scene PauseScene

# Sixty frames later the game below has not moved: it is suspended, not told
# to stop -- nothing in GameScene says "paused". Its HUD is still drawn,
# under the veil, and takes no input: a click on its Pause button does
# nothing at all.
102 click 70 105
104 expect scene PauseScene
104 shot frozen

# Resume has the focus (the pause menu's first control): the gamepad's A
# pops it, and the score goes on from where it stopped.
105 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_RIGHT_FACE_DOWN
105 expect scene GameScene
125 shot resumed

# --- the failure path: give up ----------------------------------------------

# Pause again from the keyboard -- the HUD's one button has the focus -- then
# down to Give up: change<MainMenuScene>() clears the stack, and the game's
# _end() keeps its score as the best one, which the menu shows.
126 tap KEY_ENTER
126 expect scene PauseScene
128 tap KEY_DOWN
130 tap KEY_ENTER
130 expect scene MainMenuScene
141 shot best_kept
141 end
